**Repaired Scraper Configuration**

```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "description": "Static selector scraper for GPU price",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "product_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "ID derived from the URL path",
      "extractor": {
        "type": "path",
        "pattern": "/([^/]+)$"
      }
    },
    "title": {
      "type": "string",
      "extractor": {
        "type": "css",
        "selector": "h1.product-title",
        "attribute": "text"
      }
    },
    "price": {
      "type": "number",
      "extractor": {
        "type": "css",
        "selector": ".price",
        "attribute": "text",
        "transform": [
          {
            "type": "regex",
            "pattern": "(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)",
            "group": 1
          },
          {
            "type": "toNumber",
            "trim": true
          },
          {
            "type": "absolute"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "availability": {
      "type": "string",
      "extractor": {
        "type": "css",
        "selector": ".stock-status",
        "attribute": "text",
        "transform": [
          {
            "type": "trim"
          }
        ]
      },
      "enum": ["in_stock", "out_of_stock"]
    },
    "rating": {
      "type": "number",
      "extractor": {
        "type": "css",
        "selector": ".rating-stars",
        "attribute": "data-rating"
      }
    },
    "url": {
      "type": "string",
      "extractor": {
        "type": "attribute",
        "attribute": "href",
        "selector": "link[rel='canonical']"
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["product_id", "title", "price", "availability", "rating", "url"]
}
```

**Explanation of Changes**

1. **Price Extraction & Transformation**  
   - Added a regex (`(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)`) that captures only the numeric part of the price string, discarding any currency symbols or negative signs.  
   - Converted the captured string to a number, trimmed whitespace, and then applied an `absolute` transform to ensure the final price is always positive.  
2. **Selector Adjustments**  
   - Updated the CSS selectors to point to more stable, class‑based elements (`.price`, `.product-title`, etc.).  
3. **Availability Normalization**  
   - Added a trim transform and an enum for the `availability` field to standardize “in_stock” vs. “out_of_stock” values.  

These changes eliminate the negative price issue (bug M003) while preserving the original output schema.
